TextMorph for Jetpack Compose
=============================

This library is a native Jetpack Compose port of Torph, a dependency-free
animated text component for the web.

    Torph: https://torph.lochie.me
    https://github.com/lochie/torph
    Copyright (c) 2025 Lochie Axon
    Licensed under the MIT License

The morph engine (textmorph/src/main/kotlin/io/github/dim971/textmorph/core) is
a direct port of Torph's packages/torph/src/lib: the text segmentation in
text-morph/utils/segment.ts, the place-value number segmentation in
text-morph/utils/number.ts, the segment diff in text-morph/utils/diff.ts, the
longest common subsequence in utils/lcs.ts, the animation timing in
text-morph/utils/animate.ts, number-animate.ts and replace-animate.ts, and the
spring and easing solvers in utils/spring.ts and utils/easing.ts.

Test fixtures under textmorph/src/test/resources are generated from the
published npm package so this port can be verified against upstream output.
They are byte identical to the ones in the iOS twin.
